            <ArticleTitle>Neurosurgical treatment of pain caused by cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While pain can be a most useful symptom, it becomes a problem requiring attention when it causes or increases the patient's anxiety, prevents sleep, or starts the patient on a vicious cycle of increasing doses of narcotics with concomitant depression, anorexia, and lethargy. Various surgical modalities and their indications are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
